00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:47.160
She's actually happy.

515
00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.240
She's not the only pregnant woman in the office.

516
00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:53.340
This cuts to one of my favorite talking heads.

517
00:22:53.780 --> 00:22:59.500
Also, Pam and Angela never do joint talking heads, so you and I as friends were so excited.

518
00:22:59.780 --> 00:23:02.180
Did you notice where the talking head was located?

519
00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:02.840
Yes.

520
00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.780
With the windows behind us.

521
00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:05.140
Yeah.

522
00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:07.480
I think we need to hear it.

523
00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:08.420
Oh, yes.

524
00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:13.200
Look, it's little pregs and big pregs.

525
00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:14.980
Wait, when did we start crying?

526
00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:17.280
Isn't it amazing the difference in our sizes?

527
00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.700
Well, I am a few months ahead of you.

528
00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:26.500
I'm having a child with my husband, the senator, and Pam is having a child with Jim, the great

529
00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:27.300
salesman.

530
00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:31.740
I love the great salesman.

531
00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:34.020
Here's my take on that line.

532
00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.940
I think Angela is actually trying to be nice.

533
00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:37.680
She is.

534
00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:43.100
This is her passive-aggressive way of trying to give Pam a compliment.

535
00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:43.700
Yes.

536
00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:45.060
Oh, okay.

537
00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:47.680
I have one background catch in this talking head.

538
00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:48.520
What is it?

539
00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:51.740
Did you notice that Angela's fingernails are bright red?

540
00:23:52.420 --> 00:23:52.980
No.

541
00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:56.180
When has she ever had on red nail polish?

542
00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:56.560
Oh.

543
00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:57.160
Ever.

544
00:23:57.460 --> 00:24:00.720
This is like some real spicy stuff.

545
00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:06.140
Well, I went in my digital clutter, and the week we filmed this episode, I was also

546
00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:07.680
filming Struck by Lightning.

547
00:24:08.340 --> 00:24:09.260
Oh, wow.

548
00:24:09.260 --> 00:24:13.920
And I was going back and forth between the two sets this week, and my character on Struck

549
00:24:13.920 --> 00:24:19.400
by Lightning had fingernail polish and this big updo, and I emailed you, Jenna, because I

550
00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:25.380
said this, I can't believe on one day I wear a fake belly, and then I go to the next set,

551
00:24:25.460 --> 00:24:26.600
and I wear a fake butt.

552
00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:32.100
This whole week has been fake belly, fake butt, fake belly, fake butt, because my character

553
00:24:32.100 --> 00:24:37.880
on Struck by Lightning, the director wanted her to have kind of a big derriere, and they

554
00:24:37.880 --> 00:24:40.020
had a padded butt suit I had to put on.

555
00:24:40.420 --> 00:24:41.460
Isn't this crazy?

556
00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:45.920
You spent so much time in those wetsuit padded outfits.

557
00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:46.580
Yes.

558
00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:52.300
It was a very funny week for me, because I was going back and forth, but I guess for

559
00:24:52.300 --> 00:24:54.700
this talking head, I forgot to take the nail polish off.

560
00:24:54.980 --> 00:24:58.560
Well, we got a fan question for you, Angela, from Anna S.

561
00:24:58.700 --> 00:24:59.720
in Scranton.

562
00:24:59.960 --> 00:25:01.100
What's up, Scranton?

563
00:25:01.420 --> 00:25:06.280
Anna said, Angela, I was wondering who came up with the idea for your character to be pregnant,

564
00:25:06.280 --> 00:25:11.040
and did the writers talk to you about it, or were you just surprised at the table read?

565
00:25:11.460 --> 00:25:15.980
I think Angela marrying the senator was such an interesting development for her character,

566
00:25:15.980 --> 00:25:19.000
and you do such an amazing job portraying her emotional journey.

567
00:25:19.420 --> 00:25:25.360
I do find it very interesting that she revenge-dated Andy, but now that she's with the senator,

568
00:25:25.620 --> 00:25:26.600
it seems different.

569
00:25:26.880 --> 00:25:31.640
Do you think that she really loved the senator, or was she just believing that she loved him,

570
00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:34.400
and all the time her heart belonged to Dwight?

571
00:25:34.940 --> 00:25:37.680
Well, Anna, thank you so much for your thoughtful questions.

572
00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:39.740
They did not tell me about the pregnancy.

573
00:25:40.420 --> 00:25:45.760
I found out about it at a table read, and I just remember being so delighted, because it

574
00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:46.940
was just a new thing to play.

575
00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:51.540
We'd been playing these characters for a while now, and any time you got a new layer to them,

576
00:25:51.540 --> 00:25:53.260
it was really exciting as an actor.

577
00:25:54.060 --> 00:26:01.940
And as far as Angela and Dwight and the senator, I always believed that Angela's one true love was

578
00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:03.200
Dwight, always.

579
00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:10.340
And the way I approached Angela dating and then marrying the senator was that Angela was very

580
00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:16.080
enamored with the idea of being in this sort of elite circle in society, you know?

581
00:26:16.320 --> 00:26:18.060
That was very intoxicating for her.

582
00:26:18.060 --> 00:26:18.920
It was very intoxicating.

583
00:26:19.140 --> 00:26:20.100
She loved status.

584
00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:22.640
She loved Dwight's status in the office.

585
00:26:22.860 --> 00:26:25.560
She always thought he should be the manager, you know?

586
00:26:25.740 --> 00:26:33.260
And so then to have someone who had the nice big house and had the title be interested in her,

587
00:26:33.820 --> 00:26:38.900
that was, in a way, her ultimate revenge to Dwight as well, is that she got to marry someone

588
00:26:38.900 --> 00:26:42.380
she thought, everyone thought, was very legitimate, you know?

589
00:26:42.380 --> 00:26:49.500
Um, so I think she was in love with the idea of being a senator's wife, but I don't think

590
00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:52.640
she ever truly loved him, but she loved the idea of it all.

591
00:26:53.640 --> 00:26:55.080
Yeah, I get that.

592
00:26:55.360 --> 00:27:03.220
Now, Angela, we also got a lot of mail about my body, about my pregnant body.

593
00:27:03.360 --> 00:27:04.480
What were folks saying?

594
00:27:04.700 --> 00:27:08.420
First of all, let me say, I was about eight months pregnant when we started shooting this

595
00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:08.920
season.

596
00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:18.700
And in this rewatch, when I saw myself on camera, I was like, oh my gosh, I was a real

597
00:27:18.700 --> 00:27:20.100
pregnant lady right there.

598
00:27:20.100 --> 00:27:22.260
And I felt really proud.

599
00:27:22.680 --> 00:27:24.620
I was like, look at me.

600
00:27:25.900 --> 00:27:31.940
It occurred to me, I haven't seen a lot of that on TV or in movies.

601
00:27:32.260 --> 00:27:33.080
It's true.

602
00:27:33.300 --> 00:27:34.800
They often hide pregnancies.

603
00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:35.680
They hid mine.

604
00:27:35.680 --> 00:27:36.080
Yes.

605
00:27:36.280 --> 00:27:40.880
So all you ever saw was my head popping over things or a giant bag in front of me.

606
00:27:41.140 --> 00:27:46.540
But for you in this season, you were showing your actual body going through pregnancy and

607
00:27:46.540 --> 00:27:48.360
going through your final trimester.

608
00:27:48.700 --> 00:27:48.960
Yes.

609
00:27:49.240 --> 00:27:51.740
Well, I got three fan questions to share about it.

610
00:27:51.880 --> 00:27:56.440
So the first one is from Shea J in British Columbia, who wanted to know, was there any conversation

611
00:27:56.440 --> 00:27:59.480
about attempting to hide my pregnancy for this season?

612
00:28:00.140 --> 00:28:06.160
As soon as I told Paul and Greg that I was pregnant, they asked if they could write it

613
00:28:06.160 --> 00:28:06.820
into the show.

614
00:28:07.040 --> 00:28:08.260
They thought the timing was right.

615
00:28:08.860 --> 00:28:11.020
I did not take this decision lightly.

616
00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:15.340
However, I had waited a very long time to share my pregnancy news.

617
00:28:15.340 --> 00:28:23.940
I have had close family members lose pregnancies in the later stages of their pregnancy.

618
00:28:24.260 --> 00:28:27.080
And it is like a grief.

619
00:28:27.720 --> 00:28:29.500
I know my sister.

620
00:28:29.860 --> 00:28:30.080
I know.

621
00:28:30.420 --> 00:28:30.660
Yes.

622
00:28:30.820 --> 00:28:37.860
So it's very it's very scary to put something out there like that, because if something does

623
00:28:37.860 --> 00:28:42.640
go wrong, God forbid, and then you have to continue playing someone pregnant when you

624
00:28:42.640 --> 00:28:43.400
no longer are.

625
00:28:43.520 --> 00:28:47.460
It's a terrifying and very vulnerable place to put yourself in.

626
00:28:47.640 --> 00:28:54.540
And I asked Paul, I said, if we write the pregnancy into the show and something happened,

627
00:28:55.120 --> 00:28:57.020
would something happen to Pam, too?

628
00:28:58.340 --> 00:29:01.840
Or would I have to go to work and put on some fake belly?

629
00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:03.760
Like, I don't I like I just, you know.

630
00:29:03.980 --> 00:29:04.160
Yeah.

631
00:29:05.200 --> 00:29:07.980
So Lee and I talked about it for a long time.

632
00:29:08.380 --> 00:29:14.240
And ultimately, we decided that while that is always a possibility in pregnancy, it is not

633
00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:19.020
a probability that all of my ultrasounds were pointing toward a pregnancy that was not

634
00:29:19.020 --> 00:29:19.780
going to involve any.

635
00:29:20.140 --> 00:29:20.580
Yeah.

636
00:29:20.700 --> 00:29:22.700
You know, having a healthy pregnancy.

637
00:29:22.900 --> 00:29:23.300
I was.

638
00:29:23.300 --> 00:29:25.680
So we agreed to write it into the show.

639
00:29:25.800 --> 00:29:28.620
But that was a big consideration and a big conversation, Shay.

640
00:29:28.840 --> 00:29:33.520
And I want to say that I really appreciated Paul and Greg's thoughtfulness in that conversation.

641
00:29:34.500 --> 00:29:38.920
So next, we had a fan question from Hannah L.

642
00:29:39.180 --> 00:29:41.820
in California, who said, I am pregnant with

643
00:29:41.820 --> 00:29:43.660
my second child right now and due in September.

644
00:29:43.940 --> 00:29:48.560
My body image has been so up and down during this pregnancy, as it is for so many women.

645
00:29:48.560 --> 00:29:53.080
And I would like to know, what was it like for you to be pregnant on camera?

646
00:29:53.360 --> 00:29:59.220
I cannot emphasize enough how much I love seeing Pam's second pregnancy on the show because it, of

647
00:29:59.220 --> 00:30:02.840
course, seems like such a real and accurate representation.

648
00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:08.560
As an aside, I know it can be hard to be pregnant and working a demanding job, especially with

649
00:30:08.560 --> 00:30:09.100
long hours.

650
00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:12.860
So I just want to say, on behalf of so many working moms, we see you.

651
00:30:13.600 --> 00:30:14.540
Thank you, Hannah.

652
00:30:15.320 --> 00:30:16.920
And then Haley O.

653
00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:21.940
from Texas said, having dealt with eating disorders and eating disorder

654
00:30:21.940 --> 00:30:28.080
recovery during four pregnancies and postpartum during my 20s, I love how Pam looks like a

655
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:29.260
real pregnant woman.

656
00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:34.760
Not that they can't look small, but it's just not all packaged in a perfect little area where

657
00:30:34.760 --> 00:30:36.040
the womb is all the time.

658
00:30:36.460 --> 00:30:38.960
Pregnancy can come in all shapes and sizes.

659
00:30:39.260 --> 00:30:43.960
I used to have a hangup about how other pregnant women could stay tiny except for their cute

660
00:30:43.960 --> 00:30:46.580
little bump, whereas I kind of looked big all over.

661
00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:51.000
It made my eating disorders so difficult to deal with and recovery nearly impossible.

662
00:30:51.200 --> 00:30:57.840
But still to this day, seven years after starting ED recovery, when I see big pregs, it makes

663
00:30:57.840 --> 00:30:58.640
me tear up.

664
00:30:58.800 --> 00:31:05.540
I love how Angela is snide about the sizes because it does show, in a way, how society thinks

665
00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:06.740
pregnant women should be.

666
00:31:06.900 --> 00:31:09.760
But not every body is the same.

667
00:31:11.810 --> 00:31:13.190
That is so true.

668
00:31:13.190 --> 00:31:15.970
Haley, I could not have soapboxed that better.

669
00:31:16.250 --> 00:31:16.510
Yeah.

670
00:31:17.330 --> 00:31:22.510
And Angela, in my MySpace blog, I wrote about this as well.

671
00:31:22.710 --> 00:31:23.630
Oh, let's hear it.

672
00:31:23.850 --> 00:31:25.730
I said this.

673
00:31:26.470 --> 00:31:30.370
It has been quite an adventure while working while so very pregnant.

674
00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:35.950
We've been working hard to shoot as many episodes as possible before I give birth, and that has

675
00:31:35.950 --> 00:31:39.150
basically meant that I'm working up until my due date.

676
00:31:39.590 --> 00:31:40.970
Luckily, I feel great.

677
00:31:40.970 --> 00:31:42.230
I've been very fortunate.

678
00:31:42.530 --> 00:31:47.270
I haven't had much pain at all, which I credit to my twice-weekly weight training and nightly

679
00:31:47.270 --> 00:31:48.490
walks with my husband.

680
00:31:48.910 --> 00:31:51.930
I think I had a pretty moderate pregnancy philosophy.

681
00:31:52.170 --> 00:31:53.730
I didn't starve myself.

682
00:31:53.990 --> 00:31:58.590
I didn't eat only organic greens and salads, but I was aware of what I put in my body,

683
00:31:58.590 --> 00:32:00.830
and I tried to make mostly healthy choices.

684
00:32:01.450 --> 00:32:06.310
By the way, it's good to gain weight during pregnancy, and I mean more than the Hollywood

685
00:32:06.310 --> 00:32:07.330
15 pounds.

686
00:32:07.690 --> 00:32:12.450
Not only does your body need to create a base for carrying around that giant belly, you

687
00:32:12.450 --> 00:32:14.390
need a reserve for when you begin breastfeeding.

688
00:32:14.510 --> 00:32:16.890
It all makes sense and works in harmony.

689
00:32:17.530 --> 00:32:20.310
That's not to say that I've always loved this process.

690
00:32:20.310 --> 00:32:24.630
It is a hard day when you look down and see cellulite on your shins.

691
00:32:25.250 --> 00:32:26.930
I remember that day, Angela.

692
00:32:27.150 --> 00:32:27.350
Do you remember?

693
00:32:27.490 --> 00:32:28.910
I think I texted you about it.

694
00:32:29.150 --> 00:32:30.510
I was like, really?

695
00:32:30.910 --> 00:32:32.010
My shins?

696
00:32:32.130 --> 00:32:34.670
No, I remember you actually showing me.

697
00:32:34.830 --> 00:32:36.250
I was like, wow.

698
00:32:36.770 --> 00:32:37.890
But here's what I wrote.

699
00:32:38.050 --> 00:32:41.810
I said it was one of those moments where I thought, yep, I'm really a mom now.

700
00:32:42.010 --> 00:32:46.490
This is just the first in a long list of things I'm going to do for my kid.

701
00:32:46.490 --> 00:32:48.030
So hang in there, ladies.

702
00:32:48.030 --> 00:32:49.830
We're all in this together.

703
00:32:50.550 --> 00:32:51.510
That's great.

704
00:32:51.510 --> 00:32:53.150
I love that you wrote that.

705
00:32:53.390 --> 00:32:58.910
Yeah, it was really great because it took me back to my mindset at the time, and I gained

706
00:32:58.910 --> 00:33:00.650
a lot of weight in that pregnancy.

707
00:33:01.130 --> 00:33:08.250
I was starving all the time, and I don't mean like hungry or like, oh, it's an hour past

708
00:33:08.250 --> 00:33:08.850
dinner time.

709
00:33:08.850 --> 00:33:09.730
I'm hungry.

710
00:33:09.730 --> 00:33:18.990
I mean like I had a visceral hunger that could not be quenched, and it wanted carbs.

711
00:33:19.230 --> 00:33:20.390
That is what it wanted.

712
00:33:20.610 --> 00:33:21.850
That was with my firSt.

713
00:33:22.070 --> 00:33:27.090
With my daughter, I wanted crisp, cold vegetables.

714
00:33:27.530 --> 00:33:28.590
They could not be colder.

715
00:33:28.690 --> 00:33:29.490
They could not be crisper.

716
00:33:29.670 --> 00:33:31.370
I just wanted peanut butter.

717
00:33:31.490 --> 00:33:32.970
I wanted strawberries.

718
00:33:33.510 --> 00:33:36.130
I remember just eating giant bowls of strawberries all the time.

719
00:33:36.130 --> 00:33:37.630
Here's the thing, you guys.

720
00:33:37.830 --> 00:33:41.410
I really appreciate that you wrote that, Jenna, because we both worked right up into our due

721
00:33:41.410 --> 00:33:41.790
dates.

722
00:33:42.150 --> 00:33:43.050
Many women do.

723
00:33:44.070 --> 00:33:50.370
And what you have to navigate in a day, especially in your last trimester, you're doing all the

724
00:33:50.370 --> 00:33:53.810
things everyone else is doing, but you're also growing a baby.

725
00:33:54.070 --> 00:33:54.290
Yeah.

726
00:33:54.530 --> 00:34:00.090
And so it is wonderful when people write in and say the things like what Haley said and

727
00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:05.550
Hannah said, because it feels good that we all see each other and that we all recognize

728
00:34:06.150 --> 00:34:07.650
what we do for our children.

729
00:34:07.910 --> 00:34:09.290
And lovingly so.

730
00:34:09.790 --> 00:34:10.610
Happy to do it.

731
00:34:10.730 --> 00:34:14.770
But at the same time, folks, if you are out there and your coworker is very pregnant,

732
00:34:15.010 --> 00:34:16.010
be nice to her.

733
00:34:17.990 --> 00:34:18.790
Yeah, exactly.

734
00:34:19.310 --> 00:34:23.570
And speaking of that, Angela, I did write in my MySpace blog, the cast and crew has been

735
00:34:23.570 --> 00:34:24.030
so kind.

736
00:34:24.170 --> 00:34:25.670
They've taken such good care of me.

737
00:34:25.670 --> 00:34:30.670
I have to imagine it's been good for our little guy to be around so much love and laughter

738
00:34:30.670 --> 00:34:31.510
each day.

739
00:34:31.890 --> 00:34:32.070
Yeah.

740
00:34:32.710 --> 00:34:37.170
And I did think that I think I get to go to work and this little guy is just feeling

741
00:34:37.170 --> 00:34:38.590
me laugh so hard all day.

742
00:34:38.650 --> 00:34:39.290
I know.

743
00:34:39.410 --> 00:34:42.630
I thought that, too, especially in dinner party when I was so pregnant.

744
00:34:42.630 --> 00:34:44.430
And I'm like, Isabel is in there.

745
00:34:44.770 --> 00:34:47.470
Your mom is laughing her butt off.

746
00:34:47.630 --> 00:34:47.790
Yeah.

747
00:34:48.330 --> 00:34:48.630
All right.

748
00:34:48.710 --> 00:34:51.650
That was a little bit of a long tangent, but I think an important one.

749
00:34:51.830 --> 00:34:52.210
Yes.

750
00:34:52.410 --> 00:34:53.890
We're still in the cold open.

751
00:34:54.030 --> 00:34:54.370
We are.

752
00:34:54.510 --> 00:34:55.090
Where are we?

753
00:34:55.670 --> 00:34:56.930
We OK, here we are.

754
00:34:57.350 --> 00:35:00.390
Jim and Daryl are trying to help Dwight move Kevin.

755
00:35:00.770 --> 00:35:02.930
Go to two minutes and 38 seconds.

756
00:35:03.230 --> 00:35:06.390
Leslie David Baker is completely cracking up.

757
00:35:06.430 --> 00:35:06.830
He is.

758
00:35:07.010 --> 00:35:07.650
In the background.

759
00:35:08.610 --> 00:35:09.310
Totally busted.

760
00:35:09.650 --> 00:35:12.410
I want to share with you guys something from the shooting draft.

761
00:35:12.610 --> 00:35:14.610
It's also in the deleted scenes on the DVD.

762
00:35:15.610 --> 00:35:17.470
Jim turns to Ryan for help.

763
00:35:17.750 --> 00:35:19.290
He says, Ryan, little help.

764
00:35:19.590 --> 00:35:22.310
And Ryan just looks at them and walks away.

765
00:35:23.150 --> 00:35:23.350
Wow.

766
00:35:23.550 --> 00:35:25.310
And then he has this talking head.

767
00:35:25.670 --> 00:35:30.010
Where he explains how trends make their way to Scranton.

768
00:35:30.330 --> 00:35:31.430
It's so funny.

769
00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:32.810
I'm going to put it in our stories.

770
00:35:33.130 --> 00:35:33.310
OK.

771
00:35:33.510 --> 00:35:35.350
He holds up an elaborate map.

772
00:35:35.510 --> 00:35:37.130
I'm like, when did Ryan make this map?

773
00:35:37.290 --> 00:35:39.090
Why does he care so much about trends?

774
00:35:39.090 --> 00:35:40.970
And this is his talking head.

775
00:35:41.350 --> 00:35:43.570
This is the way trends move across the country.

776
00:35:43.790 --> 00:35:44.950
They start in Japan.

777
00:35:45.690 --> 00:35:45.970
L.A.

778
00:35:46.010 --> 00:35:47.570
and New York pick it up soon after.

779
00:35:48.170 --> 00:35:50.850
Seattle looks at it and decides not to do it.

780
00:35:51.250 --> 00:35:53.050
Chicago gets it three months after that.

781
00:35:53.230 --> 00:35:55.290
Then it travels down the Mississippi.

782
00:35:55.590 --> 00:35:57.070
All the red states do it.

783
00:35:57.070 --> 00:35:59.450
Good morning, America does a piece about it.

784
00:35:59.510 --> 00:36:01.550
And then it shows up in Scranton.

785
00:36:03.010 --> 00:36:09.330
It's very funny because planking had been around for a while by the time it got to this episode.

786
00:36:09.490 --> 00:36:10.210
So that's pretty funny.

787
00:36:10.850 --> 00:36:12.870
Finally, Jim is going to say, you know what?

788
00:36:12.990 --> 00:36:14.330
No one should be planking.

789
00:36:14.490 --> 00:36:17.390
And Andy agrees and asks Dwight to take care of it.

790
00:36:17.390 --> 00:36:22.610
So Dwight walks around and basically starts pushing people off their planks violently.

791
00:36:23.010 --> 00:36:24.530
He drops things on their heads.

792
00:36:24.690 --> 00:36:26.270
He uses a fire extinguisher.

793
00:36:26.930 --> 00:36:29.570
We got a fan question from Quinty in Houston.

794
00:36:29.830 --> 00:36:32.790
How in the world did they do the planking scenes in the cold open?

795
00:36:32.950 --> 00:36:33.930
Were they stunt people?

796
00:36:34.430 --> 00:36:39.430
Especially for Kelly on the tall cabinet in Andy's office and Meredith falling off the bathroom stall wall.

797
00:36:39.570 --> 00:36:40.990
Those had to be stunt people, right?

798
00:36:41.610 --> 00:36:45.810
Well, everybody, I would normally go to Randy Cordray with this question.

799
00:36:46.050 --> 00:36:46.230
Yeah.

800
00:36:46.230 --> 00:36:51.370
But as we mentioned before, Randy moved on from the show after season seven.

801
00:36:51.810 --> 00:36:58.970
And our line producer for season eight and nine was Steve Burgess, who is a wonderful, delightful human being.

802
00:36:59.150 --> 00:37:00.070
We were so lucky.

803
00:37:00.230 --> 00:37:04.490
We had Ken Sabornak, then Randy Cordray, and then the amazing Steve Burgess.

804
00:37:04.850 --> 00:37:05.390
I know.

805
00:37:05.850 --> 00:37:08.910
Steve sends me an email for my birthday every year.

806
00:37:09.050 --> 00:37:09.490
Yeah, same.

807
00:37:09.630 --> 00:37:10.770
We're still in touch with him.

808
00:37:11.150 --> 00:37:13.410
We hit him up for details on these stunts.

809
00:37:13.530 --> 00:37:14.330
And guess what?

810
00:37:14.330 --> 00:37:18.710
But he wrote back and said it was all done by the actors.

811
00:37:19.290 --> 00:37:19.830
Yeah.

812
00:37:20.070 --> 00:37:23.590
He mentioned he thought Mindy did not love being up on the cabinet.

813
00:37:23.870 --> 00:37:24.710
He remembers that.

814
00:37:24.870 --> 00:37:29.150
But he said even Kevin, Meredith, Toby, it was all done by the actors.

815
00:37:29.330 --> 00:37:34.750
He said they had to rehearse with our stunt coordinator, Wally Crowder, on Tuesday.

816
00:37:34.750 --> 00:37:37.070
And then we shot them all on Friday.

817
00:37:37.710 --> 00:37:40.090
Well, I texted Kate Flannery about it.

818
00:37:40.210 --> 00:37:42.890
I was like, Kate, give me the dish on doing this planking stunt.

819
00:37:42.890 --> 00:37:44.890
And she sent us in an audio clip.

820
00:37:45.810 --> 00:37:48.430
Hey, that was me in the planking scene.

821
00:37:48.730 --> 00:37:52.670
Yeah, I planked on top of the stall of a men's room toilet.

822
00:37:53.590 --> 00:37:58.390
And they just had a couple mattresses on top of the toilet.

823
00:37:58.650 --> 00:38:00.030
It was kind of janky.

824
00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:08.270
And I kept thinking, I hope when rain uses the fire extinguisher that I go the right way.

825
00:38:08.830 --> 00:38:12.070
Because if I felt I fell the wrong way, I would have hit the ground.

826
00:38:13.090 --> 00:38:13.810
Risky, risky.

827
00:38:14.030 --> 00:38:19.010
But I guess, you know, at that point, I really felt like a pro.

828
00:38:19.010 --> 00:38:23.770
So watching it now, I could have gone bad faSt.

829
00:38:24.870 --> 00:38:26.610
I can't believe it, actually.

830
00:38:26.890 --> 00:38:29.170
They had a mattress over the toilet?

831
00:38:29.490 --> 00:38:32.290
Is that the toilet that maybe Warren Buffett peed in?

832
00:38:32.410 --> 00:38:33.670
Okay, well, you got to stop breathing.

833
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:40.380
I don't want to think about Warren Buffett.

834
00:38:41.680 --> 00:38:45.480
I don't want to think about Warren Buffett peeing in our prop toilet.

835
00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:48.080
But yes, probably.

836
00:38:48.580 --> 00:38:48.960
I mean.

837
00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:52.840
Also, Jenna, in the script, more people were planking.

838
00:38:53.040 --> 00:38:56.780
In the shooting draft, Gabe is going to enter for the day.

839
00:38:56.980 --> 00:39:00.300
And Hank is planking at the reception couch.

840
00:39:00.580 --> 00:39:00.820
Hank?

841
00:39:00.960 --> 00:39:01.420
Hank.

842
00:39:02.460 --> 00:39:04.460
Gabe looks at him and says, planking.

843
00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:05.120
Amazing.

844
00:39:05.420 --> 00:39:05.880
Relevant.

845
00:39:07.040 --> 00:39:12.200
He then takes a picture of Hank, letting go of a large suitcase, which falls over.

846
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:16.700
Then there was a Gabe talking head, explaining why he had returned.

847
00:39:16.880 --> 00:39:18.260
It's in deleted scenes.

848
00:39:18.260 --> 00:39:18.940
Let's hear it.

849
00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:20.700
Good morning.

850
00:39:24.000 --> 00:39:25.180
Corporate wants me up here.

851
00:39:25.640 --> 00:39:26.960
Dunder Mifflin wants me down there.

852
00:39:28.340 --> 00:39:31.860
What they worked out is Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, I'm here in Scranton.

853
00:39:32.180 --> 00:39:33.880
Tuesday, Thursday, I'm in Tallahassee.

854
00:39:34.020 --> 00:39:36.580
I mean, I feel like Vera Farmiga and up in the air.

855
00:39:36.840 --> 00:39:37.280
You know?

856
00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:38.800
More money, more probleMs.

857
00:39:39.220 --> 00:39:43.240
Although I didn't get a raise, so, you know, same money, more probleMs.

858
00:39:43.620 --> 00:39:48.940
On a mug that says, same money, more probleMs.

859
00:39:49.520 --> 00:39:51.400
That is really funny.

860
00:39:51.660 --> 00:39:55.100
So, he's just, like, taking the red eye every other day.

861
00:39:55.340 --> 00:39:57.200
He's just flying back and forth.

862
00:39:57.600 --> 00:40:01.760
Oh, you know, I wish that that talking head would have stayed in, because when I saw him

863
00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:04.100
pop up in later scenes, I was confused.

864
00:40:04.400 --> 00:40:04.560
Right?

865
00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:06.280
You're like, wait, Gabe left.

866
00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:06.900
Yeah.

867
00:40:07.180 --> 00:40:07.320
Yeah.

868
00:40:07.860 --> 00:40:08.340
Oh.

869
00:40:08.680 --> 00:40:09.840
That should have stayed in.

870
00:40:09.840 --> 00:40:14.320
Pretty much, no one wants to work with Gabe, so they just kept sitting back and forth.

871
00:40:15.600 --> 00:40:17.920
Did you notice the new opening credits, Angela?

872
00:40:18.220 --> 00:40:18.900
I did.

873
00:40:19.280 --> 00:40:22.320
Andy is going to place what looks like to be, like, a boat captain?

874
00:40:22.500 --> 00:40:22.700
Yeah.

875
00:40:22.800 --> 00:40:24.040
Like a wooden sailor guy?

876
00:40:24.060 --> 00:40:24.240
Yeah.

877
00:40:24.560 --> 00:40:28.960
But it falls off his desk when he's adjusting it, which I thought was kind of amazing.

878
00:40:29.120 --> 00:40:29.280
Yeah.

879
00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:32.740
And James Spader is up there in the credits as well.

880
00:40:33.140 --> 00:40:33.540
Yeah.

881
00:40:34.140 --> 00:40:38.800
Well, I know this is unusual, since we've only gotten through the cold open at this point,

882
00:40:38.900 --> 00:40:40.180
but I think we should take a break.

883
00:40:40.460 --> 00:40:41.740
I need to use the restroom.

884
00:40:42.300 --> 00:40:42.740
Same.

885
00:40:43.020 --> 00:40:45.220
And then we'll come back and we'll do the rest of the episode.

886
00:40:45.340 --> 00:40:46.240
Maybe I'll plank.

887
00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:48.420
Is this when you're going to plank?

888
00:40:48.920 --> 00:40:49.680
After I pee.

889
00:40:49.980 --> 00:40:50.160
Okay.

890
00:41:00.580 --> 00:41:02.800
Interesting things happened during our break.

891
00:41:02.980 --> 00:41:03.800
Yes, they did.

892
00:41:04.020 --> 00:41:05.640
Let me just share one.

893
00:41:06.320 --> 00:41:08.440
Ellie Kemper texted us back.

894
00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:10.400
I'm going to read what she said.

895
00:41:10.400 --> 00:41:17.240
Ladies, it breaks my heart to have to choose between you two, but Ange is absolutely right.

896
00:41:17.540 --> 00:41:19.280
Three exclamation points.

897
00:41:19.540 --> 00:41:24.920
There is no way, in all caps, I was planking directly on that hard concrete.

898
00:41:25.180 --> 00:41:27.280
I am certain there was some sort of pad.

899
00:41:27.520 --> 00:41:29.440
I'm strong, but not that strong.

900
00:41:29.820 --> 00:41:30.320
Ha ha!

901
00:41:30.840 --> 00:41:31.360
Yes.

902
00:41:31.540 --> 00:41:32.200
I knew it.

903
00:41:32.280 --> 00:41:33.800
All right, I stand corrected.

904
00:41:33.800 --> 00:41:36.080
And it does make sense to me now.

905
00:41:36.080 --> 00:41:40.780
Now, it makes sense to me that she did not have her forehead on a hard piece of concrete.

906
00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:41.220
Of course.

907
00:41:41.300 --> 00:41:41.860
Yes, lady.

908
00:41:42.080 --> 00:41:45.380
I mean, upon reflection for just two seconds.

909
00:41:45.960 --> 00:41:46.620
Of course.

910
00:41:46.860 --> 00:41:47.280
Of course.

911
00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:52.240
Also during the break, though, speaking of planking, Angela did plank.

912
00:41:52.640 --> 00:41:53.520
I did plank.

913
00:41:53.680 --> 00:41:55.320
I was a little confused what planking was.

914
00:41:55.380 --> 00:41:56.020
I kind of forgot.

915
00:41:56.200 --> 00:41:57.440
Remember, I was like, how do I do this?

916
00:41:57.600 --> 00:42:03.340
But then Sam and Cassie found a little green chair where they sit in sound mix, and I planked on it.

917
00:42:03.540 --> 00:42:04.380
Very well.

918
00:42:04.600 --> 00:42:05.840
You planked very well.

919
00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:06.520
Thank you.

920
00:42:06.680 --> 00:42:07.960
You held it for a long time.

921
00:42:08.300 --> 00:42:10.560
I did, because you were like, I'm going to take a picture.

922
00:42:10.720 --> 00:42:11.300
Now, I'm going to come over here.

923
00:42:11.360 --> 00:42:12.220
I was like, I'm done.

924
00:42:12.800 --> 00:42:14.000
Get me off this chair.

925
00:42:15.060 --> 00:42:15.660
All right.

926
00:42:15.780 --> 00:42:18.920
Well, we are back, and this is going to start a Pam runner.

927
00:42:19.220 --> 00:42:23.100
A very weepy Pam runner, where she's watching this commercial.

928
00:42:23.240 --> 00:42:27.700
I guess she's been watching it over and over about a dog, and he's trying to protect his bone,

929
00:42:27.740 --> 00:42:29.440
and everything about it makes her cry.

930
00:42:30.160 --> 00:42:31.360
This was a real commercial.

931
00:42:32.240 --> 00:42:33.740
I remember this commercial.

932
00:42:34.080 --> 00:42:35.480
What commercial was it?

933
00:42:35.480 --> 00:42:44.380
I feel like it was for, like, an insurance company, and it's just this dog, and he just is, like, he keeps moving his bone from place to place because he doesn't know, like,

934
00:42:44.400 --> 00:42:45.740
the safest place for it.

935
00:42:45.740 --> 00:42:46.960
Oh, my gosh.

936
00:42:47.420 --> 00:42:49.240
I can't remember if it was, like, for a bank.

937
00:42:49.640 --> 00:42:51.800
Maybe he eventually puts his bone in the bank.

938
00:42:51.920 --> 00:42:52.980
Maybe it was for a bank.

939
00:42:53.280 --> 00:42:54.520
But it was a real commercial.

940
00:42:54.940 --> 00:42:56.420
I was actually watching it.

941
00:42:56.420 --> 00:42:59.380
Now, Robert California is going to arrive,

942
00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:11.240
and I love Jim's talking head where he says that Robert California will pick someone and zero in on them and then have a super intense small talk.

943
00:43:11.600 --> 00:43:14.320
That is such a great character trait.

944
00:43:14.620 --> 00:43:14.840
Yes.

945
00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:18.820
I just – I can imagine working with someone like that and being like, oh, no, oh, no.

946
00:43:19.120 --> 00:43:20.920
Well, he's going to lock in on Erin.

947
00:43:21.220 --> 00:43:22.520
I love under her breath.

948
00:43:22.660 --> 00:43:23.420
She's like, here we go.

949
00:43:23.660 --> 00:43:23.860
Yeah.

950
00:43:24.200 --> 00:43:24.520
Okay.

951
00:43:25.200 --> 00:43:31.440
And I also love their exchange where he asks her how her day is going, and she starts by saying, well, I woke up, and he interrupts her.

952
00:43:31.580 --> 00:43:31.820
Yeah.

953
00:43:31.860 --> 00:43:33.060
He says, you don't need to say that, Erin.

954
00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:33.280
Yeah.

955
00:43:33.400 --> 00:43:34.480
Everybody wakes up, Erin.

956
00:43:34.600 --> 00:43:34.780
Yeah.

957
00:43:35.040 --> 00:43:36.140
Since the dawn of time.

958
00:43:36.680 --> 00:43:37.520
It's been happening.

959
00:43:38.220 --> 00:43:41.180
So then she says, suddenly I was awake.

960
00:43:41.460 --> 00:43:41.900
I know.

961
00:43:42.280 --> 00:43:42.580
I know.

962
00:43:43.660 --> 00:43:49.660
Andy interrupts this chit-chat with Erin to remind Robert that they had a meeting scheduled,

963
00:43:49.660 --> 00:43:55.700
and Andy's going to have a talking head where he says he has to talk to Robert about some important stuff,

964
00:43:55.700 --> 00:44:00.700
and one of those things is that he wants everybody to get their extra-long Columbus Day weekend.

965
00:44:00.920 --> 00:44:01.260
Mm-hmm.

966
00:44:02.020 --> 00:44:03.280
Well, guess what?

967
00:44:03.280 --> 00:44:11.500
But Robert California, when he goes to talk to Andy, leaves his notebook, his spiral notebook that he walks around with, jotting things down in,

968
00:44:11.620 --> 00:44:14.500
and he leaves it open at front reception.

969
00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:17.240
And Erin sees it, and there's a liSt.

970
00:44:17.440 --> 00:44:22.880
There's two columns with the line down the middle and everyone's names on either side.

971
00:44:23.160 --> 00:44:23.580
Mm-hmm.

972
00:44:23.580 --> 00:44:25.860
We had a fan catch from Evan D.

973
00:44:26.040 --> 00:44:35.840
in Buffalo, New York, who said, at 6 minutes and 20 seconds, you can see all the names on Robert's list, and instead of Creed's name being there, it just says Old Man.

974
00:44:36.100 --> 00:44:36.980
Yeah, I saw that.

975
00:44:37.720 --> 00:44:45.000
So that detail was in the script, Evan, as was that little waving standoff between Jim and Pam.

976
00:44:45.580 --> 00:44:46.880
That was scripted.

977
00:44:47.220 --> 00:44:47.400
Yeah.

978
00:44:47.400 --> 00:44:48.900
And I loved doing that moment.

979
00:44:48.960 --> 00:44:50.300
I was so excited about that.

980
00:44:50.780 --> 00:44:52.720
Well, here is how the list breaks down.

981
00:44:52.720 --> 00:44:59.140
On the left side, we have Jim, Dwight, Andy, Daryl, Oscar, Toby, Phyllis, Angela, Kevin.

982
00:44:59.840 --> 00:45:01.600
Also, someone has been erased.

983
00:45:01.840 --> 00:45:02.880
Did you notice that?

984
00:45:03.060 --> 00:45:03.220
Yes.

985
00:45:03.440 --> 00:45:03.820
There's a spot.

986
00:45:04.300 --> 00:45:10.960
On the right side, we have Stanley, Gabe, Kelly, Ryan, Old Man, Pam, Meredith, Erin.

987
00:45:11.280 --> 00:45:14.580
And two spots have been erased, I noticed.

988
00:45:14.920 --> 00:45:16.280
There's been some moving of names.

989
00:45:16.280 --> 00:45:17.140
There's been some movement.

990
00:45:17.680 --> 00:45:18.040
Mm-hmm.

991
00:45:18.480 --> 00:45:20.820
This has The Office all abuzz.

992
00:45:20.820 --> 00:45:22.820
Everyone's starting to talk about it.

993
00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:25.340
Dwight, Phyllis, Stanley, they want to know what's up.

994
00:45:25.960 --> 00:45:28.360
Pam runs over to the copier to make a copy of it.

995
00:45:28.480 --> 00:45:31.860
And Kevin says, we need a warning signal if Robert's coming.

996
00:45:32.040 --> 00:45:35.260
And Jim is like, we do not need a warning noise.

997
00:45:35.460 --> 00:45:35.740
Warning.

998
00:45:36.260 --> 00:45:36.700
Warning.

999
00:45:37.280 --> 00:45:37.720
Warning.

1000
00:45:38.080 --> 00:45:39.640
And then they all go to their spots.

